ILLUSTRATIVE CONSUMPTION
An SRE app or workflow can call the same Lens Agent API. An application input may start as text or a bounded payload. The currently documented runtime envelope carries kind=text. This is not proof of an implemented typed-payload endpoint or SDK.

INSPECTED LOCAL HELPER
scripts/kagent-a2a-invoke.sh builds JSON-RPC message/send with message.kind=message, role=user and a parts entry carrying kind=text. It invokes /api/a2a/{namespace}/{agent}/ with the required trailing slash for the inspected kagent runtime. Verify the receiving version and API before live use.

SYNTHETIC REQUEST BODY
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": "synthetic-lens-request",
  "method": "message/send",
  "params": {
    "message": {
      "kind": "message",
      "messageId": "synthetic-lens-request",
      "contextId": "synthetic-lens-context",
      "role": "user",
      "parts": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Compare the workload symptoms with related engineering work."
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

